# SHA-256 of the Joomla! full packages the integration tests install
# (tests/ci/download-joomla.sh refuses a package that doesn't match). The same
# versions have to be listed here as in the matrix tests/ci/matrix.json
# (checked by tests/lint/check-joomla-checksums.php). The workflow of com_bfstop
# installs through the same script, so a version it uses has to be listed here.
#
# Adding a version: download the package from the GitHub release, compute its
# SHA-256 and compare MD5/SHA1 with the ones on https://downloads.joomla.org
# (the page of the version lists them; it has no SHA-256), then add the line
# and say below how it was checked.
#
#  5.4.8  MD5 and SHA1 equal those on downloads.joomla.org/cms/joomla5/5-4-8
#  6.1.3  taken from the GitHub release asset (Joomla's page for the version
#         could not be consulted); check it against downloads.joomla.org
#  5.4.10  taken from the GitHub release asset by the joomla-versions workflow;
#         compare with downloads.joomla.org/cms/joomla5/5-4-10
#  6.1.4  taken from the GitHub release asset by the joomla-versions workflow;
#         compare with downloads.joomla.org/cms/joomla6/6-1-4
2c9dc7e6f451c83c43bbb7eb5c9348cb889ba802b72915c5bbd899f9d2de3f3d  Joomla_5.4.8-Stable-Full_Package.tar.gz
aa72c425105cf775312f9610598b9f1c8866c7f3219a729b59d29a56ff7f76c4  Joomla_5.4.10-Stable-Full_Package.tar.gz
184f8c582cde5981693de7c28547c6e834c48c50cb377c7b8421bbfd33bbdf6f  Joomla_6.1.3-Stable-Full_Package.tar.gz
9558a3a3754cbe798c8a8b3d46afa4e4a0a9284de876e4ce82c0ccaeb9f4af41  Joomla_6.1.4-Stable-Full_Package.tar.gz
f7a4c3962c4a8682f5847ea9d47d2848f6eb475109805935c9e19a5c6511829d  Joomla_6.2.0-Stable-Full_Package.tar.gz
